.SH NAME
CWE\-697 \- Incorrect Comparison
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product compares two entities in a security\-relevant context, but the comparison is incorrect, which may lead to resultant weaknesses. This Pillar covers several possibilities: the comparison checks one factor incorrectly; the comparison should consider multiple factors, but it does not check at least one of those factors at all; the comparison checks the wrong factor.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2020\-5849
Unraid Unraid, added 2021\-11\-03.
.PP
Unraid Authentication Bypass Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Unraid contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows attackers to gain access to the administrative interface. This CVE is chainable with CVE\-2020\-5847 for remote code execution.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-05\-03.
.PP
